Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:31:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wbemdisp: SWbemSink and the asynchronous methods of services
 and objects

SWbemSink (WbemScripting.SWbemSink) is a class with Cancel and the ISWbemSinkEvents events
(OnObjectReady, OnCompleted, OnProgress, OnObjectPut) through a connection point, with class
information that names the events as its default source. The Async methods of SWbemServices
(Get, Delete, InstancesOf, SubclassesOf, ExecQuery, AssociatorsOf, ReferencesTo, ExecMethod) and
of SWbemObject (Put, Delete, Instances, Subclasses, Associators, References, ExecMethod) run the
operation and report to the sink: OnObjectReady for each object, OnObjectPut for a Put, then
OnCompleted with the result and the context the caller gave. Something that is not a SWbemSink is
refused with WBEM_E_INVALID_PARAMETER; an operation that fails at the call fails the call.

diff --git a/dlls/wbemdisp/locator.c b/dlls/wbemdisp/locator.c
index 268b97b..f52b1bf 100644
